/* HELLFORGE v1.0.0.0 ALPHA — CORE-EXPANSION: REGAS */
// .ei project index — multi-file composition
   File:       simple_project.ei
   Version:    v4 (multi-file project) — .ei extension
   Status:     CURRENT STANDARD
   
   .ei files are multi-file project roots that use the **inherit**
   keyword to compose a larger piece from multiple part files.
   This is HELLFORGE's module/import system for organized songwriting.
   
   The **inherit** keyword imports all content from another .e file
   as if it were written inline. Inheritance is transitive:
   inherited files can themselves inherit other files.

/* @title "Simple Project" — Project metadata (optional but recommended).
   The title is used by the compiler for output naming and logging. */
@title "Simple Project"

/* @bpm 120 — Global tempo for the entire project.
   Individual parts can override with their own @bpm if needed. */
@bpm 120

/* **inherit parts/intro.e** — Import the intro melody.
   The compiler reads "parts/intro.e", parses all its content,
   and inserts it at this point in the project timeline.
   
   Paths are relative to the .ei file's directory.
   The inherited file can contain any valid E syntax,
   including loops, expressions, and even further inherit directives. */
**inherit parts/intro.e**

/* **inherit parts/verse.e** — Import the verse melody.
   This plays after the intro content completes.
   Multiple inherit lines sequence parts one after another. */
**inherit parts/verse.e**

/* After both parts are inherited, play a final resolution.
   This code runs after all inherited content. */
play chord(C, major) @dur:w @vel:ff

/* Inheritance rules:
   - A file can only be inherited once (no circular inheritance).
   - Inherited files can themselves use **inherit** (up to 5 levels deep).
   - Variables ($var) are global across all inherited files.
   - Channel assignments persist across files.
   - If no @bpm is set in the .ei, the first part's @bpm is used. */

// Run from project root: py ep.py compile samples/ei/simple_project.ei
